{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_QktPjZAJVSQ7yxZ1zp0yk4l5","content":"Title: OAuth refresh token grant type and OAuth access and refresh token expiration\nSite: Zendesk\nDate: 2025-04-30\nURL: https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/9203748839066-OAuth-refresh-token-grant-type-and-OAuth-access-and-refresh-token-expiration\nSnippet: Hi folks! I'm getting the same error as Phil and cannot figure out a way to solve it. I'm trying to introduce refresh token usage into my Zendesk OAuth workflow, but I'm encountering an \"invalid_grant\" error. I'm able to retrieve the token and use it, but not able to utilize refresh token. I'm using this doc page as a reference: https://developer.zendesk.com/api-reference/ticketing/oauth/grant_type_tokens/#create-token-for-grant-type In my authorization call, I'm passing both `expires_in` and `r\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth server token (/oauth/token/) | REST API Solution Guide\nSite: Fortinet Documentation\nURL: https://docs.fortinet.com/document/fortiauthenticator/8.0.1/rest-api-solution-guide/498666/oauth-server-token-oauth-token\nSnippet: OAuth server token (/oauth/token/) Response codes ``` Get token (Password-based) curl -k -v -X POST https://[FAC_IP]/api/v1/oauth/token/ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{ \"username\": \"luser1\", \"password\": \"12345678\", \"client_id\": \"client_id\", \"client_secret\": \"client_secret\", -> in case of confidential \"grant_type\": \"password\" }' Response: { \"access_token\": \"shrWNdu1xJRUgpcUi2bhYRX1Sl8pXe\", \"expires_in\": 0, \"message\": \"successfully authenticated\", \"refresh_token\": \"tU85BMdOoV3pktSSiLaABJ\n\n---\n\nTitle: Refresh Token not in /oauth/token payload - Auth0 Community\nSite: Auth0 Community\nDate: 2020-06-11\nURL: https://community.auth0.com/t/refresh-token-not-in-oauth-token-payload/44557\nSnippet: Jun 2020 post by XfiJSXIUvu on Jun 12, 2020 I cannot seem to get a refresh token in my call to the /oauth/token endpoint. First I authorize myself like so: ``` const redirectUrl = chrome.identity.getRedirectURL('auth0'); const clientId = \"CLIENT_ID\"; const options = { client_id: clientId, redirect_uri: redirectUrl, response_type: 'code', scope: \"offline_access\", audience: \"API_IDENTIFIER\", }; const qs = parse.qs; const domain = \"DOMAIN\"; const url = `https://${domain}/authorize?${qs.stringify(op\n\n---\n\nTitle: Zoom oauth refresh token giving { \"reason\": \"Invalid Token!\", \"error\": \"invalid_grant\" } - API and Webhooks / Authentication - Zoom Developer Forum\nSite: Zoom Developer Forum\nDate: 2024-04-14\nURL: https://devforum.zoom.us/t/zoom-oauth-refresh-token-giving-reason-invalid-token-error-invalid-grant/107870\nSnippet: Heading link Steps I followed: FIrst we are checking if the user exist in our db if the user does not exist, then we will call the API: `https://zoom.us/oauth/authorize?client_id=6wG1sdT5QOyC3As57R4SA&response_type=code&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3000/de/user/redirect/zoom&code_challenge=` After allowing the access, I am getting the code which I use to call the oauth/token API and get the access and refresh token: Endpoint: `https://zoom.us/oauth/token` Request: code: `` grant_type: authoriza\n\n---\n\nTitle: \"Invalid Token!\" error message when trying to refresh oauth token - API and Webhooks - Zoom Developer Forum\nSite: Zoom Developer Forum\nDate: 2020-05-15\nURL: https://devforum.zoom.us/t/invalid-token-error-message-when-trying-to-refresh-oauth-token/13363?page=3\nSnippet: post by tmswartz12 on May 19, 2020 Thanks for the response. I am able to get it to work locally for a bit. So it leads me to believe that it doesn’t have to do with my database storage of the token… I just tried again and the error persists… Using my PROD keys (not published or reviewed yet). It seems like my refresh_token is invalid. Steps to reproduce… 1. POST ‘ https://api.zoom.us/oauth/token’ with grant_type ‘authorization_code’ and the code passed from the redirect. - Response = access_toke\n\n---\n\nTitle: Oracle API Gateway OAuth User Guide\nSite: oracle.com\nDate: 2015-07-27\nURL: https://docs.oracle.com/cd/E65459_01/user.1112/E65456_01.pdf\nSnippet: When an authorization code or access token request is received from a client application, the API ... https://127.0.0.1:8089/api/oauth/token). The ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: openclaw_oauth_sync/docs/HOW-TOKEN-REFRESH-WORKS.md at main\nSite: git.eeqj.de\nDate: 2026-03-01\nURL: https://git.eeqj.de/ROOH/openclaw_oauth_sync/src/branch/main/docs/HOW-TOKEN-REFRESH-WORKS.md\nSnippet: Anthropic OAuth Token Lifecycle Claude Max subscriptions use OAuth tokens for API authentication. - Access token ( ``): Used for API requests, expires in ~8 hours - Refresh token ( ``): Used to get new access tokens, long-lived - Token endpoint: `POST https://console.anthropic.com/v1/oauth/token` - Client ID: `9d1c250a-e61b-44d9-88ed-5944d1962f5e` (Claude Code public OAuth client) How Claude Code CLI Refreshes Tokens Claude Code CLI has built-in token refresh. Before each API request: 1. Checks \n\n---\n\nTitle: API Documentation - oauth/token - Geoloqi Developers\nSite: geoloqi.com\nURL: https://developers.geoloqi.com/api/oauth/token\nSnippet: Contents - 1URL - 2Description - 2.1Parameters - 3Password - 3.1Parameters - 4Authorization Code - 4.1Parameters - 5Refresh Token - 5.1Parameters - 6Application Token - 6.1Parameters - 7Assertion - 7.1Parameters - 8Response - 8.1Success - 8.2Error URL https://api.geoloqi.com/1/oauth/token Description Request an access token from the Geoloqi OAuth system. This method may be called with the following grant_types: - authorization_code - an auth code received upon the redirect from the authorize ste\n\n---\n\nTitle: Sign in with CoinPay (OAuth 2.1)\nSite: CoinPay\nURL: https://coinpayportal.com/docs/oauth\nSnippet: /api/oauth/authorize, Authorization endpoint (response_type=code only). POST, /api/oauth/token, authorization_code, refresh_token, device_code grants. POST, / ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API Reference: Introduction\nSite: surveydynamix.com\nDate: 2016-02-19\nURL: https://apidocs.surveydynamix.com/\nSnippet: To refresh a access token using a refresh_token use this code: curl -X POST \"https://surveydynamix.com/api/oauth/token\" -d \"grant_type=refresh_token\" -d ...\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
