{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_jaJA3YjwYRaZ9dhgtKqOE6Ks","content":"Title: long-run-hybrid-coach/README.en.md at main\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-08-13\nURL: https://github.com/atomchung/long-run-hybrid-coach/blob/main/README.en.md\nSnippet: ACTIVITY:READ, Read your completed training. WELLNESS:READ ... Intervals does offer a read-only settings scope ... Intervals.icu OAuth support. After Intervals ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: inspectIntervalsPermissions 回報的是發證當下的紀錄，不是 provider 現在認不認\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-08-18\nURL: https://github.com/atomchung/long-run-hybrid-coach/issues/162\nSnippet: inspectIntervalsPermissions 當下回： [\"ACTIVITY:READ\", \"CALENDAR:WRITE\", \"SETTINGS:READ\", \"WELLNESS:READ\"] ， settings_read: \"readable\" 。\n\n---\n\nTitle: kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSite: Github\nDate: 2024-01-01\nURL: https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSnippet: ... intervals.icu/oauth/authorize'); authUrl.searchParams.set('client_id ... set('scope', 'ACTIVITY:READ ACTIVITY:WRITE WELLNESS:READ'); authUrl.\n\n---\n\nTitle: @kuranov/intervals-client\nSite: npm\nDate: 2026-02-03\nURL: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@kuranov/intervals-client\nSnippet: Examples OAuth2 Flow For public applications serving multiple users, implement the full OAuth2 authorization code flow: ``` // Step 1: Redirect user to authorization URL const authUrl = new URL('https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize'); authUrl.searchParams.set('client_id', YOUR_CLIENT_ID); authUrl.searchParams.set('redirect_uri', YOUR_REDIRECT_URI); authUrl.searchParams.set('response_type', 'code'); authUrl.searchParams.set('scope', 'ACTIVITY:READ ACTIVITY:WRITE WELLNESS:READ'); authUrl.searchPa\n\n---\n\nTitle: Fitbit Web API returns 410 Gone: how to keep sleep, HRV and weight flowing into intervals.icu\nSite: DEV Community\nDate: 2026-11-03\nURL: https://dev.to/antivex/fitbit-web-api-returns-410-gone-how-to-keep-sleep-hrv-and-weight-flowing-into-intervalsicu-11la\nSnippet: Route 3. Any phone: read the Google Health API yourself The setup for google-health-to-intervals takes about 20-30 minutes, once: 1. Create your private copy with Use this template. 2. Create a Google Cloud project and enable the Google Health API. 3. On the consent screen: - choose External and leave the publishing status on Testing; - add yourself as a test user; - add three read-only scopes: `googlehealth.sleep.readonly`, `googlehealth.health_metrics_and_measurements.readonly` and `googleheal\n\n---\n\nTitle: rowsandall/rowing-courses-spec.md 位于 develop\nSite: Wereldraadsel Git\nDate: 2026-03-16\nURL: https://git.wereldraadsel.tech/sander/rowsandall/src/branch/develop/rowing-courses-spec.md\nSnippet: Stage 1 — Course library and CrewNerd integration 1.4 Authentication and API key issuance (Stage 1) Login flow: 1. User visits the course browser and clicks \"Sign in with intervals.icu\". 2. Worker redirects to `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=...&scope=PROFILE_READ,ACTIVITY_READ&response_type=code`. 3. intervals.icu redirects to `GET /oauth/callback?code=...`. 4. Worker exchanges code for tokens and fetches the athlete profile ( `GET /api/v1/athlete/self`) to confirm identity and\n\n---\n\nTitle: Connect Strava, Garmin, COROS: Import Your Workouts\nSite: Trainingload.ai\nDate: 2026-09-06\nURL: https://www.trainingload.ai/docs/guide/connect-third-party-platforms\nSnippet: Connect COROS 1. Open Connections → COROS and complete OAuth authorization. 2. After the card shows connected, select Sync activities to reconcile workouts. 3. Select Sync daily on web, or Sync health now on mobile, to reconcile supported daily or health data. 4. Check the last-sync state and any error shown on the card. COROS deliberately exposes separate activity and daily-data actions. A successful activity sync does not prove that the health reconciliation also ran. If the COROS card is not \n\n---\n\nTitle: What's New\nSite: PlanWatts\nURL: https://planwatts.cc/docs/en/whats-new\nSnippet: v0.9.3 — ATP Sync with Intervals.icu, Plan Editor Overhaul & Docs Portal Plan Editor Overhaul The plan editor got a complete rework. The main additions: AI generates workouts at three levels: - Full plan — fills all phases at once - Per phase — click the sparkle icon on any phase header - Per week — click the sparkle icon on any week's target cell The AI matches your weekly TSS target, adapts intensity to the phase type (easy aerobic in Base, threshold intervals in Build, race-pace in Peak), and\n\n---\n\nTitle: Sign in with SweatStack - SweatStack developer docs\nURL: https://docs.sweatstack.no/learn/authentication/sign-in/\nSnippet: Send users straight to one provider ¶ Add `integration=` to the authorization URL to skip the sign-in chooser and send the user straight to one provider. Use it when your app supports a single wearable, or when you want your own per-provider buttons (\"Connect Intervals.icu\", \"Connect Wahoo\") instead of one SweatStack button. Tell the user they're connecting through SweatStack This path sends the user straight to the provider, and the provider's own permission screen (Wahoo's, for example) asks t\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Page 8 - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=8\nSnippet: The app need to have WELLNESS:READ scope for the athlete to get at wellness data. Your app only has ACTIVITY:READ for that athlete. The ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2023-02-24\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=14\nSnippet: Feb 2023 post by Ken_Dolbey on Feb 24, 2023 Hi guys, I feel like I am going crazy just trying to Auth and use my API key - I constantly get 403 or 422 errors when using what appears to be a valid API key an Athlete ID - Would it be possible to just post what you are using in Python to simply authorize and call a list of your last 5 workouts? I tried the below but I feel like a moron it’s not working - all my other API auths seem to work pretty easily this one I just can’t figure out (newbie scri\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
